```

In this revised version, the `distances` dictionary is used to keep track of the shortest distance found so far to each node. The priority queue (`unvisited_nodes`) is only updated with new distances if a shorter path to a node is found. The heap invariant is maintained by always pushing new tuples onto the heap rather than updating existing ones in place. This ensures that `heappop` will always retrieve the correct minimum distance tuple.
